#/target

Cargo.lock
*.odg#
*.ods#


# Upstream reference clones (if ever added here) -- never committed.
/upstream_source/*/

# V&V raw data -- the hand-written .md write-ups in verification_and_validation/
# are committed; standalone .csv data files they reference are not.
/verification_and_validation/*.csv

# Machine-generated V&V reports, written by the diagnostic tests in
# src/backward_eqn_chebyshev_experimental/tests/. Regenerable in seconds with:
#
#   cargo test --release -p tampines-steam-tables --lib backward_eqn_chebyshev_experimental
#
# They are output, not source -- the committed .md files above are hand-authored,
# these are not, and they carry a "do not hand-edit" banner saying so.
/verification_and_validation/generated/

# Generated output of the `steam_table_plotter` example (GitHub issue #26).
# Regenerate the whole directory in a few seconds with:
#
#   cargo run --release -p tampines-steam-tables --example steam_table_plotter -- --export-all
#
# It is ignored by default because the four PNG/PDF/SVG figure sets plus their
# curve and reference-point CSVs run to tens of megabytes, and every byte of it
# is reproducible from the command above. If a particular figure is wanted as a
# committed publication artifact, add that one file with `git add -f`.
/figures/
